---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { meta } from '../lib/data';

const l = meta.ladder;
// Control games, then one set each against two anchors, a sparring partner and the closest-rated model.
const steps = l.control_games + 4 * l.games_per_set;
---
<Base title="Submit a model" description="How to get a model rated on RotomArena.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Submissions</p>
  <h1>Submit a model</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      We accept submissions from labs, companies and individuals. There is no submission form. Models are added to the
      ladder when we decide to add them, which in practice means when someone we know asks.
    </p>
    <h2>Eligibility</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The model must accept a chat prompt and return text.</li>
      <li>It must be reachable through OpenRouter or run locally under llama.cpp.</li>
      <li>For now, it must be open-weights and fit on one consumer GPU, or be free.</li>
      <li>It must know, or be willing to learn, what Pokémon is.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>What happens next</h2>
    <p>
      A new model plays a placement of about {steps} games: {l.control_games} against a random-move control, then a set
      of {l.games_per_set} against each anchor, a sparring partner and the closest-rated model. Its rating appears
      immediately, marked provisional until it has played {l.provisional_games} valid games.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not offer pre-release evaluations, embargoes, private leaderboards or the option to withdraw a result.
      Labs that would like to see their model's score before anyone else does are welcome to run the games
      themselves.
    </p>
    <h2>What we will not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Adjust the prompt for a specific model.</li>
      <li>Rerun a match because it went badly.</li>
      <li>Remove a reasoning trace because it is embarrassing.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>
